## US-016 — Exportar Reporte de Proyecto a PDF

I found an existing `GeneratePdfButton.jsx` ("Generar Informe de revisión", tutor-only) that met only part of the criteria. I reworked it into a full project-report export available to **both students and tutors**.

### Changes
- **`frontend/src/components/GeneratePdfButton.jsx`** — rewritten:
  - Button label → **"Descargar PDF"**
  - Professional header with **university logos** (`logo_carrera` + `logo_universidad`), inserted with `addImage(..., "MEDIUM")` compression to optimize image size (keeps PDF well under 10MB)
  - Includes **title, description, itinerary, dates, tutor, students**
  - **Documents table** with version + **states** (Revisado / Pendiente de revisión)
  - **Tutor comments table** (pulled from each document's populated `comments`)
  - **Metadata block**: generation date, generated-by, and **SHA-256 integrity hash** (via `crypto-js`, over a canonical JSON of the report content) — also embedded in PDF properties (`keywords`)
  - New props: `project`, `documents`, `generatedBy`
- **`frontend/src/pages/ProyectoDetalle.jsx`** — imports `useAuth`, shows the button for `canReviewDocuments || canUploadDocuments`, and passes `documents` (which already carry populated comments) + `generatedBy`.
- **`frontend/src/components/__tests__/GeneratePdfButton.test.jsx`** — 4 new tests.

### Acceptance criteria
- ✅ Botón Descargar PDF en vista de proyecto
- ✅ PDF incluye título, descripción, lista de documentos, estados, comentarios tutores
- ✅ Formato profesional con logo universidad
- ✅ Metadatos: fecha generación, generado por, hash de integridad
- ✅ Tamaño < 10MB (imágenes con compresión MEDIUM)
- ✅ `npm run lint` passes (0)
- ✅ `npm run typecheck` passes (0)

Full test suite: **25/25 passing across 7 suites**. No commits created (per workflow).

